Bluetooth: btusb: Add USB ID 37ad:0600 (TP-Link UB600, RTL8761BU)

Backport of upstream commit bc597f0cc44f0b173c50ee986a047219cd559ee9
(landed v7.2-rc1) onto the rpi-6.6.y pin. The UB600 is the same
RTL8761BU as the UB500, but ships under TP-Link's own vendor ID
instead of Realtek's. Without a quirks_table entry BTUSB_REALTEK is
never set, btrtl never uploads rtl_bt/rtl8761bu_fw.bin, and the chip
stays in ROM-only mode: hci0 appears, scanning finds nothing.

The stock linux-firmware blob runs the chip as Bluetooth 5.1 rather
than the advertised 6.0; irrelevant for A2DP (Classic), which is all
this appliance uses.

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -715,6 +715,8 @@
 
 	/* Additional Realtek 8761BUV Bluetooth devices */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x2357, 0x0604), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
+						     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH },
+	{ USB_DEVICE(0x37ad, 0x0600), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
 						     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH },
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x0b05, 0x190e), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
 	  					     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH },
